WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.850
You've made up your mind, then?

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.160
Yes.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.910
Then I shall head to the Mononokean.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.360
I'm sorry.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.540
I wish I could go.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.890
I heard the Mononokean has a new employee.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.470
I was just thinking I'd like 
a chance to see his face.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.870
Please be careful.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:25.850
Oh?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.500
I smell rain.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.330
It will rain tonight.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.800
If you say so, then it must be true.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.100
Fuzzy!

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.860
<b>Mystery 11 "The Purple Sun"</b>

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.980
I'm so glad you're back to normal!

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.990
He's so happy, he's crying.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.610
Stop being such a crybaby. It's annoying.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.990
My tear ducts are so loose, 
I can't control them!

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.190
If Fuzzy is back to normal, 
then Yahiko must be, too.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.500
Dad.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.320
<i>Zenko's dad!</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.880
What time do you kids think it is?

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:45.630
And what were you doing in 
this dark, deserted place?

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.040
He's really pissed! What should we say?

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:49.990
Huh?

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.570
Hold Fuzzy for a second.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.160
What's wrong?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.840
I just strained my back.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.820
I didn't feel anything when I left the house...

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:02.820
Abeno?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.580
Get away from there, Yahiko.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.080
Aw, you found me.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.190
Yahiko!

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.250
That was your doing, Yahiko?

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.420
Haruitsuki, not only am I back to 
normal, but I can also transform.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.930
Let's play now!

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.050
That's right, you were giant, too. I forgot.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.320
What?! Ashiya, you piss me off!

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.110
I hate you!

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.430
Sorry, sorry. Anyway, get off him.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.430
No!

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.960
Don't give me that!

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.350
You have to get off him!

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.670
I'll carry you instead!

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.250
Not you! I want Haruitsuki!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.950
Stop struggling! I'll drop you!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.430
Kid, who are you talking to?

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:43.950
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:45.660
Abeno-san...

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.710
Don't look at me.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.330
The pain disappeared?

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.340
I've always talked to myself a lot...

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.090
I, um... wasn't talking to anyone just now.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.780
<i>Come to think of it, when I was stricken 
by the mysterious "laughing disease,"</i>

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.090
So, well... Don't worry about it too much.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.250
<i>this kid showed up and...</i>

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.840
Did you just cure my lower back pain?

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:06.560
Huh?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.720
Can you cure high blood pressure, too?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.110
You should get that one checked at the hospital.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:16.090
Just "that one"? So you did cure my pain!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.800
Shouldn't we help Hanae?

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.280
Huh?!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.930
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.930
Didn't you?!

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.860
<i>If I tell him it was yokai again, 
he'll think I'm kidding around!</i>

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.360
Dad, actually...

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.430
Hanae can sense spirits.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:32.490
He removed the ghost on your back.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.660
Ghost?!

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.280
You can see ghosts?

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.390
A-And it was on my lower back?

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:44.780
Um... Yeah, it totally was!

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:48.460
And a really nasty one, too!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.400
Dad can't sense spirits at all,

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.170
A n-nasty one?!

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.770
which makes him all the more 
freaked out by them.

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:54.590
Y-Yeah! Oh, but I got rid of it, so don't worry!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.120
That's what my mom said.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.270
I'm amazed he became a monk.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.070
Come work at the temple.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:04:59.900
What?!

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.450
Sometimes people come to the 
temple requesting exorcisms.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.030
All right?

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.670
Wait a minute! Abeno-san!

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.000
Hanae's calling you.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.140
Haruitsuki, let's play.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.140
Not my problem.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.210
Your name is Ashida, right?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.040
It's Ashiya.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.790
Huh? Zenko, what's going on?

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.420
That's unusual.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.290
Did something good happen?

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:20.810
Yeah.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.550
Just a little.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:28.300
It's only a little, but 
I'm glad my dad and Hanae

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.920
are getting along better.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.740
Anyway, what were you doing here with Zenko?

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.060
Um...

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.790
Are they?

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:37.510
Yeah.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.650
It's raining.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.150
Let's hurry home.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.280
And Yahiko, I'm not playing with you.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.070
Aww...

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.320
The rain doesn't seem like 
it's stopping anytime soon.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.700
I'm glad we got back before 
it really started pouring.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:58.140
That old man wouldn't let you go.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.960
That wasn't my fault.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.020
I wasn't expecting rain, 
so I didn't bring an umbrella.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.440
It'd be great if you'd give me 
a lift home, Mononokean.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.470
Okay, for 100 yen per trip.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.470
You charge for that?

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.100
I'm just kidding ~

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:18.390
You have a guest.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.660
A guest? We don't have 
any appointments today.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.350
Go greet him.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.350
Coming.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.710
Welcome.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.100
Hello.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.990
It's raining a lot in the mundane 
world today, isn't it, Mononokean?

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.780
Okina-dono.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.370
Abeno-san, get a towel and some warm tea.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.480
Sorry to drop by unannounced.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:43.390
Not at all.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:47.850
I accidentally fell into a puddle 
while walking in the rain.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:54.510
My, how terrible.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:52.700
Abeno-dono, the skies won't clear up today.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:53.880
Really?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.910
Are you the new employee?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.770
Yes. My name is Ashiya.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:03.900
My name is Inogaratake 
Yuuhi Takino Okinagami.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.700
What? "Kami"?

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.540
You're a god?!

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:14.220
I'm just an old yokai granted the 
excessive title of "god" by humans.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.330
Call me Okina.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.290
Okina-sama is worshiped at a 
shrine in the Mundane World.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.290
Then have you always lived in 
the mundane world, Okina-sama?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:29.900
I've selfishly requested to stay here.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.800
Now then, that brings us to the 
matter at hand, Abeno-dono.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.200
There's a yokai waiting 
for us near the shrine.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.060
There must be some reason 
you didn't bring them here.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:46.320
She can't use her eyes on her own.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.640
Her eyes?

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.650
Okina-dono, what exactly does that mean?

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.760
She's able to see by taking 
the vision of humans

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.370
who can see yokai.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.820
Humans just like yourself, Abeno-dono.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.020
It's nothing to scowl about.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:13.460
She only wants to be exorcised 
to the Underworld.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.440
Forgive my indiscretion.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:19.200
Besides, she only borrows a person's vision

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.860
for a couple of days, 
and then it's returned to them.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.560
Then I humbly accept your request.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.040
I told her we'll go once the skies clear.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:35.340
For today, I'll just have another 
cup of tea before I leave.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.620
You can stay as long as you'd like.

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:44.300
Really? Then perhaps I'll make 
myself at home a bit longer.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.000
Those sound like Okina-sama's footsteps.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:54.800
And...

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.550
There are two others.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.100
Thanks for waiting.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.360
You must be Abeno-dono of the Mononokean.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.440
And you must be Tomori-dono, our client.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.620
Yes. I appreciate your assistance.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.820
Certainly.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.030
I heard another person's footsteps.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.780
It's his employee, Ashiya-dono.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.140
I see. So you are...

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.310
Nice to meet you.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.670
Nice to meet you, Ashiya-dono.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:28.220
Tomori-dono, getting straight to the point,

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:31.290
there's not enough space here to 
open a portal to the Underworld.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.690
Would it be possible for us 
to move somewhere else?

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:35.930
Very well.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:37.970
I'll help you.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:40.550
A human?

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.310
So you can see, Ashiya-dono?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.540
It's been so long.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.190
So there are still humans like 
you in the mundane world.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.660
How long have you been unable to see?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.960
Who knows? It's been quite a while.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.830
Lately, I haven't met any 
humans who can see, either.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:06.890
But I remember all the sights I've seen.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.620
The mundane world is beautiful.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.960
I love this world.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:16.470
However, it's become difficult 
for me to stay here.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:22.170
And I'm just a bit hopeful that, 
once I return to the Underworld,

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:24.540
I'll be able to see normally.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.100
I see. So that's how it is.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.230
<i>He's glaring.</i>

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:34.980
Um, Tomori-san, I'd like you 
to answer me honestly...

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.240
Before you go to the Underworld,

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:40.490
would you like to see 
this world one last time?

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:41.640
What?

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:46.800
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to imply that.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.310
Please don't worry about me, Ashiya-dono.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.680
No, no! It's nothing like that at all!

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.230
It's just that if I didn't ask, 
I knew it would bother me later.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.510
B-Bother?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.640
I thought that maybe you just 
couldn't bring yourself to ask,

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:06.010
and that would make me regret not offering.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.890
Besides, this may sound patronizing,

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:14.890
but if it just means I won't be able 
to see yokai for a few days,

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:18.200
I guess I thought it would be okay, you know?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.090
<i>He's not saying anything... 
Does that mean it's okay?</i>

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.790
If I'm honest,

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:35.290
I would like to see this world once more.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:40.520
May I take your sight?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:47.010
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.420
Ashiya-dono, please close your eyes.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:52.250
Okay.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:21.370
Huh? Tomori-san?

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:26.260
Oh, right. I can't see them anymore.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:28.470
Can Tomori-san...

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.940
really see now?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.670
You should go home now.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:35.950
What? But I—

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.910
Someone who can't see yokai 
would only get in my way.

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:42.150
Yeah, but there must be a better 
way you can phrase that.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.850
I did that so Tomori-san—

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:45.000
You'll step on the furball.

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:46.660
Huh?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.280
Sorry, Fuzzy!

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.980
You can return to work once
you can see them again.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.230
Just go home for today.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.080
Okay. I guess I'll leave, then.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.430
Tomori, can you see?

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:14.680
Yes.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.730
The flowers, the dirt, the water...

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.690
So many colors are shining so brightly,

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.850
they're almost blinding.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.450
Abeno-dono.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.950
Please tell Ashiya-dono,

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.440
"Thank you so much."

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:38.340
"Now I can go to the Underworld 
without any regrets."

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:40.950
I will.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:45.720
I'm home.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.220
Welcome back.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.920
Huh? What's wrong?

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.470
What do you mean?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.460
Nothing. Never mind.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.230
Is he a bit down?

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:06.110
<i>I miss not being able to see 
Fuzzy and the Mononokean...</i>

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:11.000
<i>But it's just for a few days.</i>

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.560
<i>I'll see them again soon.</i>

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.760
Purple coneflowers.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:29.260
In the language of flowers, 
they mean "I will heal your pain."

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:31.600
What are you talking about, Mom?

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:33.010
I'm totally fine.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:35.890
You do seem fine.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:38.660
Well, I'm off.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.450
See you later.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.860
<i>That's good.</i>

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:47.080
It's finally been three days.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.360
What a long three days!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:53.370
Fuzzy! I can't wait to 
squeeze your beautiful fur!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.820
Abeno-san?

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:01.120
You're unusually early today.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.840
And you're even awake.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:07.130
Oh! I bet you were worried about 
whether my vision came back, huh?

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:10.280
You can't see him.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.130
Huh?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.090
Is Fuzzy here?

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.410
Yeah. He just jumped onto you.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:18.770
I can't see him...

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.270
I can't see him! Why not?

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.520
We'll just have to see how it goes.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.570
Sorry, Fuzzy...

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.030
<i>Two more days after that...</i>

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:37.530
The left!

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:41.130
Wrong. The answer is on top of your head.

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:42.080
What?!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.120
Fuzzy's on my head?!

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.090
Hey, wait! That's not fair!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.660
If you could see him, you 
wouldn't have fallen for it.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.700
Today's test is over.

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:56.480
Why? It's been five days,

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:58.180
but I can't see them at all.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:02.350
I can't imagine Okina-sama or 
Tomori-sama lied to me, either.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.230
Not only that, but you can't even hear them.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:06.860
Huh? Hear them?

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:09.050
Nothing. Never mind.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.280
What am I going to do?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.320
I can't even see or touch Fuzzy!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.370
Isn't there some way to restore my sight?

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.870
Is Fuzzy still on my head?

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:20.920
Ashiya.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:21.800
Yes?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.370
That's enough.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.130
What do you mean?

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.300
You should quit.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.060
I'll keep you on until 
I find my next employee.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:39.640
But...

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:43.110
I don't have any business 
you can help with right now.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:47.960
Since I've got work to do, 
I can't get complacent.

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.440
And I'm not patient enough 
to accommodate people

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.280
I might not be able to use.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.310
<i>"Might not be able to use"?</i>

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.760
<i>It's only been five days.</i>

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:03.430
<i>I've only been unable to 
see them for five days...</i>

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.340
Now that you can't use me, 
you're throwing me away?

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:18.140
I suppose I can't help you if I can't see yokai,

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:23.390
and it'd be more convenient for 
you to hire a new employee,

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:26.270
but being treated that way

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.520
still pisses me off.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:31.500
I didn't want to do this at first.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.900
I was saddled with debt, 
scared to exorcise yokai,

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:39.080
and I didn't know what to do.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.230
I wanted to quit as soon as possible.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:43.620
But it's different now.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:46.410
I'll learn to see them again, and I'll be back.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.670
I'll come back...

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:53.620
and make you bow and beg me to 
work at the Mononokean again!

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:55.800
Huh.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:01.390
Well, to make that happen, 
you'd better work real hard.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.680
What happened to your face?

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.910
Ashiya hit me with his shoe!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:22.920
Huh?

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:25.340
I hate Ashiya!

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.520
Hanae did?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:29.960
Fusshi, what'd you get?

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.860
A croquette, throat drops, and coffee.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.800
I should've gotten a croquette, too.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.860
Ashiyan, you're not buying anything?

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.410
I'm not hungry.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:40.110
You're not your perky self, either.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.240
This wilted Ashiyan looks like he needs fluids.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.700
Have some coffee.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.070
Fusshi, you're so nice. Thank you.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:48.730
You can have this, too.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:49.430
<b>Part-Time Jobs with High Pay</b>

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:50.220
Saga...

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:52.060
<i>Job ads?</i>

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.810
Use that to find a new job.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:58.140
I haven't been fired... yet.

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.600
But it's just a matter of time, right?

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.720
Well, it depends on me.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:06.310
Why don't you join a club instead of working?

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.310
A club, huh?

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.020
You can join the photography club.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.900
Want to join too, Saga?

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.200
<i>Before I started high school,</i>

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.460
I'm kind of interested.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:14.730
<i>I was excitedly thinking 
about all the possibilities.</i>

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.670
Let's go take pictures together sometime.
I'll lend you a camera.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.490
<i>But I didn't have time for 
those thoughts anymore.</i>

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.260
What kind do you want to take?

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.120
Hmm... Scenery might be nice.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.740
Oh, I know the perfect place, then.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.050
<i>Maybe I'll join a club.</i>

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:24.360
Yeah? Let's go sometime.

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:27.340
"Simultaneous inequalities"

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:30.560
refers to a set of two 
or more inequalities...

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.230
<i>Did Abeno-san take the day off?</i>

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:34.610
<i>Did he get a job on short notice?</i>

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.860
<i>Not that I care what that 
heartless employer is up to.</i>

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.020
<i>But now that I know yokai exist,</i>

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.120
<i>I hate not being able to see them.</i>

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.940
<i>I won't give up that easily.</i>

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.630
Are you sure, Itsuki?

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:56.380
I've made my decision.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:19:59.830
I'll be back later.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:08.970
Hey.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:12.730
Itsuki! Koura-sama, it's Itsuki!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.650
Itsuki's here!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:18.600
Oh, my. You came so soon this time.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.530
Don't worry.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.290
We made extra this time so

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:25.550
what happened before wouldn't happen again.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:26.510
Thanks.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:30.010
The screeching yokai seemed 
to be doing a lot better, too.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:31.130
Really?

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:33.600
He misses you and Ashiya.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:37.640
Oh? Speaking of which, he and 
his little friend aren't with you.

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:42.440
I knew it seemed too quiet. 
Ashiya's not here.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:43.760
I left him behind.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.460
Is Ashiya doing well?

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.000
I wanted to see him.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.390
It's too bad, isn't it?

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.000
He has such nice ears.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:55.540
My ears are so much better. So much better.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.400
Shizuku.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:57.930
What?

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.440
Is the Legislator around?

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.900
My brother? He's at Newt Lake.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.900
You have business with the Legislator?

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:09.380
No, I thought I'd stop by and 
see him, as long as I'm here.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.010
I'll be back.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:14.590
What? Itsuki, you're leaving already?

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.060
Sorry, Shizuku.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:18.170
Sorry I couldn't stay longer, Koura.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.040
Don't worry about it.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:23.390
You can visit for longer next time.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:25.300
With Ashiya-kun.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:34.180
Itsuki's going to see the Legislator 
without being asked?

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:37.130
How unusual.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:47.390
Long time, no see...

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:48.700
But not really, I guess.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Time "The Separation"</b>

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:29.340
Hey, Zenko, how do you have Yahiko 
help around the temple?

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:31.760
I brush his hair, feed him snacks,

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.240
and take him for walks when he gets bored.

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:36.700
And sometimes, when he feels 
like it, he cleans the temple.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:39.300
So he's 90% pet and 10% helper?
